WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.064
To test IBC,

00:00:04.144 --> 00:00:08.208
the authors assembled six sparse-reward
environments spanning both manipulation and locomotion.

00:00:08.288 --> 00:00:12.352
Two of them, Tabletop Manipulation and Sawyer Door,
come from EARL,

00:00:12.432 --> 00:00:16.497
an established benchmark for autonomous
reinforcement learning.

00:00:16.577 --> 00:00:20.641
The other four are Fetch Pick and Place, Fetch
Push, Fetch Reach, and Point-U-Maze,

00:00:20.721 --> 00:00:24.785
which are standard MuJoCo-based OpenAI Gym tasks
that the authors modified for the reset-free,

00:00:24.865 --> 00:00:28.929
non-episodic setting.

00:00:29.009 --> 00:00:33.073
Evaluation follows the EARL protocol: the agent is
spawned once,

00:00:33.153 --> 00:00:37.217
interacts continually, and is reset only rarely,

00:00:37.297 --> 00:00:41.362
after hundreds of thousands of steps.

00:00:41.442 --> 00:00:45.506
Performance is measured as the deployed policy
evaluation metric,

00:00:45.586 --> 00:00:49.650
reported at ten-thousand-step intervals and
averaged across five random seeds.
